0..74 Comment "// The hole rust-lang/rust 164250 names: a struct\'s bound `T : \'static` is"
75..154 Comment "// checked when `Q(None)` is built and assumed by its destructor; the covariant"
155..235 Comment "// assignment `q.0 = Some(&l)` then re-instantiates `Q` at the local\'s lifetime,"
236..315 Comment "// and the destructor stores a view of `l` where only a `\'static` value may go."
316..396 Comment "// Here the region a slot keeps is part of the slot\'s type, a built value\'s type"
397..478 Comment "// never changes under it, and a destructor is a region\'s end action that reaches"
479..560 Comment "// only what the region keeps: the write is refused before anything runs (#1492)."
561..563 Comment "//"
564..641 Comment "// What the hole is made of: evidence in two currencies. A bound written on a"
642..720 Comment "// type\'s definition is a side condition outside the value, re-proved at every"
721..799 Comment "// explicit use (a call, a coercion) but inherited as an assumption by the one"
800..879 Comment "// consumer with no use site, the destructor — an explicit `Drop` must repeat"
880..961 Comment "// the type\'s bounds exactly and so assumes them, and the generated drop glue has"
962..1041 Comment "// none — while subtyping by variance changes the type beneath it and nothing"
1042..1122 Comment "// re-establishes the bound. The same shape is the ergonomic rule \"bounds on the"
1123..1201 Comment "// impl, never on the struct\": a bound on the definition is re-stated on every"
1202..1281 Comment "// implementation and constrains every use. Here a constraint is a field of the"
1282..1359 Comment "// value\'s record, carried and projected, never implied from a definition and"
1360..1435 Comment "// never assumed by an implementation; the region is that field for a slot."
1437..1468 Comment "// Early exit\'s host interface."
1469..1475 Keyword "import"
